A provider references a type that does not type-check (Widget is undefined). The
loader tolerates the type error, but the invalid type would surface in the
generated signature, so plumb rejects rather than emit code that cannot compile.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrInvalidType
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

//plumb:build
func New() Widget { return Widget{} }
